WEBVTT

00:10:28.499 --> 00:10:32.044
around the year 250 AD,

00:10:32.086 --> 00:10:36.173
the city of Teotihuacan,
in the valley of Mexico,

00:10:36.215 --> 00:10:40.052
with a population
of around 100,000 people,

00:10:40.094 --> 00:10:45.224
turned its back on pyramid temples
and human sacrifices

00:10:45.224 --> 00:10:48.143
and reconstituted itself

00:10:48.185 --> 00:10:55.109
as a vast collection of comfortable villas
housing most of the city's population.

00:10:55.984 --> 00:10:59.947
When archaeologists first
investigated these buildings,

00:10:59.988 --> 00:11:01.824
they assumed they were palaces.